# Import without burning Cursor quota

Cursor weekly quota is charged for agent model turns and tool loops, not for fetching `t.me` or writing D1/R2. Bulk import must not be orchestrated inside a long Cloud Agent session.

## Hard chat boundary (no exceptions)

Agent chat / MCP / conversation may carry **only**:

- Exact aggregate counts (ready / review / rejected / unknown / skipped / written / failed)
- Short status lines (script started / exited / path to report on disk)
- Exact totals persisted to agent memory (`/cursor/stores/self/...`)

**Never** load into chat, MCP tool args, or PR/commit messages:

- Per-row usernames, titles, descriptions, tags, categories
- SQL statements, seed dumps, report JSON bodies
- Avatar bytes / base64 / R2 object bodies
- Model prompts, clef-omni payloads, or preview post text
- Grey-lexicon hit lists longer than a category name

All row work stays in local files under `/tmp/...` or the repo scripts. Read those files with tools only to drive scripts; do not paste their contents back to the user.

## Do

- Run import/seed/classify/retry scripts locally or in CI. The agent may start a command and report a short **count-only** summary.
- Follow `import-quality.mdc` before any D1 write (gates and omi inside the script, not in chat).
- Default: write D1 rows first; leave media to the refresh cron unless the user asked for avatars with the import — then `seed.ts --remote` / local fetch→R2 so bytes never pass through dialogue.
- Prefer keyword taxonomy; call `@cf/cloudflare/clef-omni` for blank categories and borderline quality only (Workers AI, not Cursor).
- Keep agent sessions short: start the paced job, stop watching; open a new short session later to read counts from the report file / memory.

## Do not

- Do not drive entries through the agent by pasting SQL, profiles, or media into the dialogue.
- Do not use Cloudflare Browser Rendering (or Puppeteer/Playwright on Workers) for public `t.me` pages. Plain HTTP fetch with a browser UA is enough.
- Do not use chat MCP for bulk D1/R2 writes when wrangler is available.
- Do not sit in one Cloud Agent for hours watching an import finish.
- Do not burst t.me or Workers AI: concurrency 1 and delays for quality/retry passes.
